course: dictionary
lesson: 12879
title: Making sure with ensure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ensure means to make certain that something happens or is true. «Please ensure the door is locked» means: make sure the door is locked before you leave.
explain: Ensure is a formal word. You will often see it in instructions and exam papers. «Ensure your name is on every page» tells you to put your name on every page, and it means exactly what it says.
explain: Ensure is often used with safety and success. «Wear your helmet to ensure your safety» means wearing it makes sure you stay safe. When you meet ensure, try swapping in make sure. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Ensure means to make certain that something happens or is true.
fact: Ensure is a formal word, common in instructions and exam papers.
fact: You can swap ensure for make sure: «Please ensure the door is locked» means «Please make sure the door is locked».
fact: Useful phrases: ensure that, ensure safety, ensure success.
fact: In science, you keep things the same to ensure a fair test.
exercise: «Please ensure the door is locked.» What does ensure mean here? | *Make certain the door is locked | Open the door wide | Paint the door | Knock on the door
exercise: The exam paper says «Ensure your name is on every page.» What should you do? | *Make sure your name is on every page | Write a poem on the page | Ask a friend to write your name | Tear the page out
exercise: «Check your work to ensure that every answer is right.» Which words could replace ensure without changing the meaning? | Forget | Guess | Hide | *Make sure
test: «Wear your helmet to ensure your safety.» What does ensure your safety mean? | Stop your safety | Show off your safety | Ignore your safety | *Make certain you are safe
test: Scientists keep things the same to ensure a fair test. What does ensure mean here? | Guess the answer | Stop the test | *Make certain the test is fair | Change everything
exam: «Ensure your answers are written in pen.» What does ensure mean? | Throw your pen away | Draw a picture of your answers | Write in pencil | *Make sure your answers are in pen
